+# Fälligkeitsdatum für Todos Implementation Plan
+
+> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.
+
+**Goal:** Todos get an optional `dueDate`, the API can filter overdue todos, and the list page shows the date, an "überfällig" marker and a "nur überfällige" filter.
+
+**Architecture:** The overdue rule lives only in `src/store.mjs` (`list({ overdue: true })`, with an injectable `today()`). `src/app.mjs` maps `?overdue=true` onto it. The page loads `/todos` and `/todos?overdue=true` and marks todos by id (spec approach A).
+
+**Tech Stack:** Node 24, `node:http`, `node:test`, plain HTML + module script. No dependencies.
+
+**Spec:** `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-01-due-date-design.md` (Ticket #1)
+
+## Global Constraints
+
+- Zero dependencies, Node builtins only.
+- Validation errors are `ValidationError` from `src/store.mjs` → HTTP 400.
+- TDD: failing test in `test/` first.
+- `dueDate` is `"YYYY-MM-DD"` or `null`, always present on every todo.
+- Overdue = `done === false` and `dueDate < today` (UTC). No date → never overdue.
+- Only `overdue=true` is accepted; any other value of `overdue` → 400.
+- No per-todo overdue field, no sorting, reminders, styling, or editing on the page.
+- New UI elements: `data-testid` `todo-due`, `todo-overdue`, `overdue-filter`. Copy: `überfällig`, `nur überfällige`.
+
+## Review Focus
+
+- Non-string `dueDate` (number `20261105`, `true`) → 400, not stored. (Task 1)
+- Impossible or malformed dates: `"2026-02-29"`, `"2026-13-01"`, `"2026-1-5"` → 400. A real leap day, `"2028-02-29"`, is accepted. (Task 1)
+- Boundary: `dueDate === today` is not overdue, and a done todo with a past date is not overdue. (Task 1)
+- `PATCH` with only `dueDate` leaves `title` and `done` unchanged, and `dueDate: null` clears it. (Task 1)
+- `?overdue=` (empty) and `?overdue=TRUE` → 400. (Task 2)
+
+---
+
+### Task 1: Store – dueDate, validation, overdue filter
+
+**Files:**
+- Modify: `src/store.mjs`
+- Create: `test/store.test.mjs`
+
+**Interfaces:**
+- Produces: `createStore({ today } = {})`. `today: () => string` (`YYYY-MM-DD`) defaults to `() => new Date().toISOString().slice(0, 10)`.
+- Produces: `store.list({ overdue } = {}) → Todo[]`. With `overdue: true` only overdue todos are returned, otherwise all of them.
+- Produces: `store.add({ title, dueDate })`, where `dueDate` is optional and defaults to `null`. `store.update(id, patch)` accepts `dueDate` (`string | null`).
+- Todo shape: `{ id, title, done, dueDate }`.
+
+- [ ] **Step 1: Write failing tests in `test/store.test.mjs`** (use `createStore({ today: () => '2026-11-01' })`)
+  - `add defaults dueDate to null`: `add({ title: 'A' })` deep-equals `{ id: 1, title: 'A', done: false, dueDate: null }`.
+  - `add accepts a valid dueDate`: `add({ title: 'A', dueDate: '2028-02-29' }).dueDate === '2028-02-29'`.
+  - `rejects invalid dueDate`: for each of `'morgen'`, `'2026-02-29'`, `'2026-13-01'`, `'2026-1-5'`, `20261105`, `true`, both `add({ title: 'A', dueDate: v })` and `update(1, { dueDate: v })` throw `ValidationError`.
+  - `update sets and clears dueDate`: after `update(1, { dueDate: '2026-10-01' })`, title and done are unchanged. After `update(1, { dueDate: null })`, `dueDate === null`.
+  - `list({ overdue: true })`: with todos due `'2026-10-31'` (open), `'2026-11-01'` (open), `'2026-10-01'` (done), `null` (open), only the first one is returned. `list()` returns all four.
+
+- [ ] **Step 2: Run** `node --test test/store.test.mjs`. Expected: FAIL.
+
+- [ ] **Step 3: Implement in `src/store.mjs`.** Helper `validDueDate(value)`: `null` is allowed. Otherwise the value must be a string matching `/^\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2}$/` **and** round-trip through `new Date(value + 'T00:00:00Z').toISOString().slice(0, 10) === value`. Otherwise throw `ValidationError('dueDate must be a YYYY-MM-DD date or null')`. Overdue: `!todo.done && todo.dueDate !== null && todo.dueDate < today()` (string comparison).
+
+- [ ] **Step 4: Run** `npm test`. Expected: store tests PASS. `creates and lists todos` in `test/app.test.mjs` now fails on the missing `dueDate`. Update its expected value to `[{ id: 1, title: 'Milch kaufen', done: false, dueDate: null }]`, then `npm test` passes completely.
+
+- [ ] **Step 5: Commit**: `git add src/store.mjs test/ && git commit -m "feat: dueDate on todos with overdue filter in store (#1)"`
+
+### Task 2: API – `GET /todos?overdue=true`
+
+**Files:**
+- Modify: `src/app.mjs`
+- Modify: `test/app.test.mjs`
+
+**Interfaces:**
+- Consumes: `createStore({ today })` and `store.list({ overdue })` from Task 1.
+- Produces: `GET /todos?overdue=true` → 200 with the overdue todos. `overdue` with any other value → 400.
+
+- [ ] **Step 1: Write failing tests.** Change `withServer(fn)` to `withServer(fn, store)` and pass the store to `createApp(store)`. Tests with `createStore({ today: () => '2026-11-01' })`:
+  - `filters overdue todos`: POST `{ title: 'alt', dueDate: '2026-10-31' }` and `{ title: 'neu', dueDate: '2026-11-02' }`. `GET /todos?overdue=true` → 200, titles `['alt']`.
+  - `rejects other overdue values`: `?overdue=false`, `?overdue=`, `?overdue=TRUE` → 400 each.
+  - `rejects an invalid dueDate over HTTP`: POST `{ title: 'A', dueDate: 'morgen' }` → 400.
+
+- [ ] **Step 2: Run** `node --test test/app.test.mjs`. Expected: FAIL.
+
+- [ ] **Step 3: Implement in `src/app.mjs`.** In the `GET /todos` branch: if `url.searchParams.has('overdue')` and the value `!== 'true'`, throw `ValidationError('overdue must be "true"')`. Otherwise `send(200, store.list({ overdue: url.searchParams.has('overdue') }))`.
+
+- [ ] **Step 4: Run** `npm test`. Expected: all PASS.
+
+- [ ] **Step 5: Commit**: `git commit -am "feat: GET /todos?overdue=true (#1)"`
+
+### Task 3: List page – date, marker, filter
+
+**Files:**
+- Modify: `public/index.html`
+- Modify: `test/app.test.mjs` (`serves the list page`)
+
+**Interfaces:**
+- Consumes: `GET /todos` and `GET /todos?overdue=true` from Task 2.
+
+- [ ] **Step 1: Write the failing test.** Extend `serves the list page` so it also matches `/data-testid="overdue-filter"/` and `/nur überfällige/`.
+
+- [ ] **Step 2: Run** `npm test`. Expected: FAIL.
+
+- [ ] **Step 3: Implement in `public/index.html`.** Add `<label><input type="checkbox" data-testid="overdue-filter"> nur überfällige</label>` above the list. The script fetches both lists, builds `overdueIds = new Set(...)` and defines `render(todos)`. For each todo it renders title (✓ unchanged), then `<span data-testid="todo-due">` with `todo.dueDate` if it is not null, then `<span data-testid="todo-overdue">überfällig</span>` if the id is in `overdueIds`. Spans are separated by a space. The checkbox `change` handler re-renders with the overdue list or with all todos.
+
+- [ ] **Step 4: Run** `npm test`. Expected: all PASS.
+
+- [ ] **Step 5: Commit**: `git commit -am "feat: show due date and overdue filter on list page (#1)"`
